<Page title="Univariate maximum likelihood"><img class="hero-logo" src="/logo.svg" alt="univariateML: a pipe with expanding normal-density smoke" width="155" height="180"/><p class="eyebrow">One variable. A mathematical library.</p><h1>Distributions,<br/>with their details.</h1><p class="summary">univariateML fits univariate distributions by maximum likelihood, and evaluates densities, probabilities, quantiles and random draws.</p><p>The portable, header-only C++17 core owns the numerical methods. R provides a thin binding; Python and JavaScript bindings are planned.</p><p><a href="/distributions/">Explore the 98 distribution papers →</a></p><h2>Read the method, know the limits.</h2><p>Each paper brings together the definition, parameter domains, fitting restrictions, implementation and decision history. A numerical check, a regression fixture and a mathematical proof establish different things.</p><p><a href="/articles/">Read the articles</a> · <a href="/search/">Search the library</a></p></Page>
